{
  // GENERATED by native/scripts/sync-vendor.js — edit that script, not this file.
  //
  // Minimal tsconfig for the vendor/ subtree, for exactly the same reason
  // native/src/tsconfig.json exists. Vitest's oxc transformer resolves a
  // tsconfig per file by walking UP from that file; for anything under vendor/
  // the first one it meets is native/tsconfig.json, which `extends`
  // "expo/tsconfig.base" and therefore only loads when native/'s own npm deps
  // are installed. native/ is a separate npm project from the pnpm root, and a
  // git worktree only symlinks the ROOT node_modules — so in any worktree that
  // walk-up fails and every test importing a vendored module dies with
  // "[TSCONFIG_ERROR] ... Tsconfig not found". That was 11 of 32 test files,
  // reported as a smaller *passing* suite (205 tests instead of 378) rather
  // than as missing coverage. CI hid it by running native's `npm ci`.
  //
  // vendor/ is framework-free TypeScript — no JSX, no decorators, no path
  // aliases — so the transform needs nothing beyond the language level.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "strict": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true
  }
}
